  "checklist": [
    "1. Division Overview (o): the banner shows '30 Divisions', the battalion count, 'Active in 1 Theater(s)' and the special forces count; the rail at the right holds the 14 modifiers in one column and the 5 division types in one column. If the tiles run in a row instead, note it (the fallback is the build's two header rows).",
    "2. Hover three modifier tiles, a division type chip, a row's bars, its level and its army shield: each tooltip shows.",
    "3. Click a division type chip: the list shows that type only; click it again to clear. Type a name into the filter box: the list narrows.",
    "4. Click each of the four sort buttons over the list.",
    "5. Scroll the division list to its end: the scrollbar runs between the list and the rail, and the last row is whole above the panel's foot.",
    "6. Navy Overview (p): count the modifier tiles in the rail (vanilla's grid showed 7; the code adds 9 or 10, GUL-044, so 2 or 3 more may show) and the ship chips; the region of each fleet whole. Press shift+l: Sunk Ships opens beside the panel at x 890; press it again or Escape to close it. Click a ship chip: does it filter?",
    "7. Air Forces Overview (l): 14 modifiers and the plane chips in the rail; click a plane chip: does it filter? Press shift+l on this tab: note whether anything happens (the button is hidden here).",
    "8. Shift+i: Equipment Details beside the panel at x 890, next to the rail.",
    "9. error.log: no 'Could not find' line, no line naming zz_1440p_army_overview.gui or GFX_1440p_AO."
  ],
  "_note": "Surveyed on 2026-10-08. A6 (2026-10-14): the panel is 900 wide; the header containers have no margin, so the file says where their widgets are. Redesign of 2026-10-16: a banner card and a rail of cards; rows of 738, 34 division rows in view (rows start at screen y 234)."
